Z||000000||MooCow||09-20-2001||12:38 AM||||I know there was a picture on here that someoen had one windshield wiper.  I think it was Travis (1fst2m6) that has only one.  Any one know how to do this and how involved it is??  Might consider doing that this winter after my car gets painted again and suspension work.<P>Thanks Ken<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_7.jpg"> <BR>87 GT, 3.4 engine with a 4:10 tranny, and Viper Yellow!||||reg||5
Z||000001||sqoach||09-20-2001||12:45 AM||||Sure, it's easy! Just take one of them off (prefferably the passenger side so the driver can still see)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><P>------------------<BR>-Adam<BR><FONT COLOR="BLUE">sqoach@yahoo.com</FONT><BR>          <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach.gif">     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/halfpole.gif">          <BR>^^^^^^<B>new project</B>^^^^^^<BR><LI><FONT SIZE="1">84 SE (FOR SALE)*SOLD(?)*<BR><LI>85 Coupe (parts car)($50)*sale pending*<BR><LI>86 SC</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||MooCow||09-20-2001||12:53 AM||||No, No, No, not like that you goof  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">.  I want it in the middle.  I kind of like the way it looks cause it is different.  Anyone know how??<P><BR>Thanks Ken||||reg||12
Z||000003||Nashco||09-20-2001||02:25 AM||||I'm interested in this kind of mod too!  The idea isn't too complex, it's just a matter of knowing how hard it is to get the linkages set up.  If somebody has done this, I'd love to see and hear how they did it!<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||SLYGUY||09-20-2001||02:28 AM||||Mercedes-Benz does it with most of their sedans. <P>Very complicated mechanicals with this. The blade actually REACHES towards the center of the windshield as it swings, and retracts to a shorter length as it wipes the passengers side of the windshield. Then it does the same on the way back. <P>You could wreck into the car watching the wiper do this as it is driving towards you.<BR>Really cool.<P>No, I haven't seen it done either. Closest I have seen on a non MB is someone put a huge wiperblade from a van or an SUV or something. Doesn't work as well I can only imagine, but looks pretty cool.<P>Just my $.02<P>Sly||||reg||1
Z||000005||FieroJoe||09-20-2001||10:34 AM||||The cheapo way is to take off both of them, and then have a big one on the middle shaft.  You'll have to angle it so when the wipers are off the blade is about in the middle so when you turn them on it swings over enough to wipe the driver's side.  Looks kinda wierd that way, I don't like it.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Joe Torma||09-20-2001||10:58 AM||||Uniwiper?  Smells like a ricer to me! J/K<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Maybe you can change the length/position of the drive rod in the cowl to get the center wiper to wipe how you want.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/simplesig1.gif">   <BR>Did you get your car in my book yet????<BR> <A HREF="http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm</A><p>[This message has been edited by Joe Torma (edited 09-20-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||Philphine||09-20-2001||11:21 AM||||i've done it. probaly the easiest way (if not quite kosher) is to take both off. get the next size up wiper blade (possibly two sizes up but i didn't try that)  and use it on one of the stock arms on the middle wiper mechanism. from what i've noticed thats all a lot of people do. <P>with the wipers off in their rest position point the arm and blade about at the upper passenger side corner and let it wipe once to check the sweep. you'll probaly have to reposition it a few times to get a satisfactory sweep and since your not changing any linkage the passenger side will have a big unswept area. thats only a problem in really big snows till the defroster warms up (sometimes rain too but it has to be a real gully washer). but again, since you didn't change any linkage if you have a lot of snow to deal with you can always go back to two wipers through the winter.<BR>i've had my '87 like that for a few years. no problems. <P>------------------<BR>Phil T.<P>start where you are,<BR>use what you have,<BR>do what you can.||||reg||1
Z||000008||DaRkLoRD||09-20-2001||08:32 PM||||could always go find one off a bus, and swap the blade for one better suited to the fiero windshield..<P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||1
Z||000009||Jncomutt||09-21-2001||07:21 AM||||On the Honda CRX, I just take off the driver side wiper and reposition the passenger side so it rests a bit higher than usual.  Thats how a lot of my friends have done it.  (the reason you see the hondas with only 1 wiper but has it halfway up the window)  I'm not sure how this would carry over to a Fiero, but I see no difference...well, Except the rice =)||||reg||1
